From c70dc396ce4315335386351787aa0efeb5b89078 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:03:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: implement core 1 "Single" schedule mode, stop
 starving sysmodules

1.0-era titles (no CPU time in the exheader) run core 1 in "Single"
mode, which was unimplemented and fell back to the Multi limiter.

Worse, the kernel's own override table marks some of those titles as
exempted from preemption (CPU time 10000): Nintendo 3DS Sound, Star Fox
64 3D, Super Monkey Ball 3D, Doctor Lautrec and Pro Yakyuu Spirits 2011.
The limiter treated 10000 as a percentage: the application phase lasted
200ms and the sysmodule phase got a negative length, so LLE sysmodule
threads on core 1 practically never ran. With the online LLE modules
on, Nintendo 3DS Sound waited forever for frd:u, which never registered.

- Only CPU time values 1..89 turn preemption on (0 disables it,
  10000 and above means exempted), matching the 3DS kernel.
- Single mode now uses 25ms slices: the application gets cpuTime%,
  sysmodules (90 - cpuTime)%, and the last 10% goes to other threads.
  Timings follow Luma3DS's notes (sysmodules/pm/source/reslimit.c).
- The "Unimplemented Single schedule mode" warning is replaced by an
  info line with the chosen mode and CPU time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
